# Production incident (2026-09-18) — history, so nobody re-adds a redirect rule here without
# reading this first. The same-origin auth proxy (Safari third-party-cookie fix; see
# netlify/edge-functions/auth-proxy.mjs) went through three attempts:
#   1. netlify.toml [[redirects]] with an (invalid) `context = "..."` field — silently
#      discarded entirely, total login outage on every browser.
#   2. The two rules moved to THIS file, ahead of the catch-all below (this file is processed
#      before netlify.toml, which is why attempt 1's rules never had a chance either way) —
#      fixed the 404s, but Netlify's declarative redirect/rewrite engine does not reliably
#      relay Set-Cookie headers back to the client, so refresh_token/CSRF cookies still never
#      reached the browser. Confirmed against Netlify's own support forum/docs.
#   3. netlify/edge-functions/auth-proxy.mjs — full programmatic control over the Response,
#      including Headers.getSetCookie() to relay cookies correctly. This is the one that
#      actually works, and it runs BEFORE this file's rules are even considered (Edge
#      Functions execute first in Netlify's request chain), so it does not need a rule here.
#
# Old domain -> hudhudnest.com (SEO audit, 2026-10-03). realestateworld.world is still attached to
# this Netlify site as an alias and served the whole app with a 200, i.e. a complete duplicate of
# hudhudnest.com. Each rule below is a host-based 301 (the trailing "!" forces it even though a
# file/rewrite could match), and MUST stay above the SPA catch-all at the bottom: this file is
# processed top to bottom and the first match wins (the same ordering trap documented above).
# Edge functions still run first for /properties/* and /sitemap.xml; on this host the property
# one now emits the production URL as canonical (resolveCanonicalOrigin).
https://realestateworld.world/*      https://hudhudnest.com/:splat   301!
http://realestateworld.world/*       https://hudhudnest.com/:splat   301!
https://www.realestateworld.world/*  https://hudhudnest.com/:splat   301!
http://www.realestateworld.world/*   https://hudhudnest.com/:splat   301!
#
# Legacy German-named listing URLs (/wohnungen, /wohnungen/:id). Angular used to redirect these in the
# browser only (200, then a client-side route change), so a crawler saw a duplicate page and a social
# crawler got an empty preview. A real 301 here consolidates them onto /properties. Must stay above the
# SPA catch-all. (QA Phase 20, P20-D05.)
/wohnungen        /properties         301!
/wohnungen/:id    /properties/:id     301!
#
# /download is NOT an Angular route: it is a static page generated at build time
# (tools/generate-download-page.mjs -> public/download/index.html) so it works without the app shell
# and the QR code can point at one stable address. The explicit forced rewrite keeps `/download`
# (no trailing slash, which is what the QR encodes) answering 200 on that page whatever Netlify's
# directory handling does, and must stay ABOVE the catch-all below. Do not add /download to
# deep-links.config.json paths: the installed app would then open this page instead of the store.
# Legal pages (2026-11-13): one privacy policy at /privacy-policy (in four languages) and the Impressum at /impressum.
# The old German privacy draft and the earlier /imprint address answer with a real 301 so links and crawlers follow.
/datenschutz   /privacy-policy?lang=de   301!
/imprint       /impressum                301!
/download   /download/index.html   200!
#
# /download/android: the stable address for the direct APK download. The block below is rewritten by the build
# (tools/generate-download-page.mjs) from downloads/android-release.json: an approved release redirects to its one
# validated address; with none it returns to /download. Do not edit it by hand.
# BEGIN generated:download-android (tools/generate-download-page.mjs; edit downloads/android-release.json instead)
/download/android   https://github.com/Naeem-Ba/HudhudNest-Releases/releases/download/v1.3.0/HudhudNest-1.3.0.apk   302!
# END generated:download-android
#
# Research surveys (market validation, 2026-11-22). Static single-file pages, not Angular routes: the forced rewrites
# keep /survey/<name> (with or without a trailing slash, query string kept in the address bar for ref/UTM) answering
# 200 with the survey file, and must stay ABOVE the SPA catch-all below. No redirect happens, so links shared on
# WhatsApp keep their parameters.
/survey/offices    /survey/survey-offices.html   200!
/survey/offices/   /survey/survey-offices.html   200!
#
# Original rule — SPA fallback. Load-bearing since hash-based routing was removed (see
# ARD-Wohnungsmieten.md ADR-001): every in-app route (/properties/:id, /auth/verify-email, …) is
# now a real path the server receives directly, so EVERY one of them depends on this rule to get
# the app shell instead of a raw 404 — not just a stray non-hash URL anymore.
/*    /index.html   200
